  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "With **T'AU EMPIRE** as your [Army Faction](vsdata:core-rule/select-army-faction), as [your Shooting phase](vsdata:core-rule/shooting-phase) begins, you can pick any of your units that have this ability; they become Observer units.\n\nIn [your Shooting phase](vsdata:core-rule/shooting-phase), each Observer unit of yours that is **eligible to shoot** and has yet to be **selected to shoot** in the phase, other than **FORTIFICATION** and **[Battle-shocked](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock)** units, picks a **[visible](vsdata:core-rule/visibility)** enemy unit to mark as its Spotted unit for the rest of the phase. An enemy unit can become a Spotted unit only once per phase.\n\nYour units with this ability that are not Observer units count as Guided units while they target any Spotted unit. Whenever a model of yours in a Guided unit attacks a Spotted unit, the attack gets +1 BS, and also gets **[[IGNORES COVER]](vsdata:weapon-ability/ignores-cover)** if the Observer unit that marked that Spotted unit has **MARKERLIGHT**, for the rest of the phase.",
